Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.13,0:00:03.16,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Scarlett's disappeared.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.09,0:00:07.39,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,It's been two days \Nsince I've seen His Lordship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.79,0:00:13.02,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,I thought she went away because \Nshe exhausted herself back then,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.19,0:00:15.81,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,but now I'm sure I was wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.07,0:00:22.02,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Did she get "fed up" with me, as they say?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.15,0:00:25.65,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,Constance Grail. You have a visitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.97,0:00:30.21,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,You ungrateful girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.67,0:00:33.72,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,Think about what you've put me through.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.04,0:00:38.11,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,One day, out of the blue, \NI hear my daughter's been arrested,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.11,0:00:42.55,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,so I rush back to the capital \Nonly to find her slated for execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.55,0:00:44.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I... I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.47,0:00:48.78,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,What on earth is going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.01,0:00:51.24,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Father...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.65,0:00:56.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Please disown me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.97,0:01:02.69,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What if blame were to spread\Nto our family because of me?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.69,0:01:05.41,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,I don't know much about palace intrigue.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.26,0:01:10.51,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,I don't know what's happening \Nin this country, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.51,0:01:11.63,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.05,0:01:16.43,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,I think I can at least take a stand\N to keep my daughter safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.88,0:01:19.38,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But consider the risks!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.38,0:01:21.50,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,Listen, Constance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.50,0:01:26.44,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,Nothing inspires us like other people,\N no matter the era.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.98,0:01:31.10,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,We have our own ways of doing things.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.36,0:01:35.52,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,"Be you sincere."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.45,0:01:41.02,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,I'm glad to see you looking well.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.00,0:01:49.28,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Here you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.28,0:01:50.37,Default,Child A,0,0,0,,Thanks!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.33,0:01:58.26,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,What do you want with me, Shoshanna?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.84,0:02:00.92,Default,Shoshanna,0,0,0,,Change the people keeping watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.92,0:02:01.88,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.60,0:02:03.99,Default,Shoshanna,0,0,0,,They get rough.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.41,0:02:11.31,Default,Shoshanna,0,0,0,,Who knows what they'll do \Nif someone stands up to them?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.30,0:02:16.02,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,So be it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.74,0:02:33.42,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Kiriki kirikuku.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.42,0:02:35.62,Default,Lookout A,0,0,0,,L-Lie low and stay calm.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.04,0:02:37.78,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Kindly withdraw.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.18,0:02:45.39,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,What do you want with us?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.66,0:02:49.35,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I came to warn you, brave little lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.03,0:02:53.28,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Unless you want to die, \Nkeep your head down.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.09,0:02:56.03,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,You're awfully kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.03,0:02:57.02,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Kind?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.46,0:03:00.50,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Yes. You and Shoshanna both.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.49,0:03:04.66,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I'll kill you if ordered to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.66,0:03:08.25,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,I know. And that's why you came, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.25,0:03:10.72,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,To make sure you won't get that order.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.45,0:03:13.74,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,To make sure I'm not killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.02,0:03:27.05,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,I don't believe it!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.05,0:03:30.29,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,Connie, kidnap a prince of Faris?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.80,0:03:33.81,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,And now she's to be publicly executed?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.10,0:03:36.01,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Say, Mylene,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.01,0:03:41.19,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,wasn't public execution abolished \Nafter Scarlett Castiel?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.64,0:03:43.79,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Do you know why?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.79,0:03:47.79,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,Yes. I believe a citizens' \Ngroup protested.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.79,0:03:49.96,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,The Violet Association, \NI think it was called.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.28,0:03:52.02,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,The Violet Association?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.02,0:03:53.46,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Thank you, Mylene.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.46,0:03:55.53,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,Huh? Where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.53,0:03:58.46,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,To save Connie, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.81,0:04:02.37,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,You can't expect me \Nto just sit around weeping.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.71,0:04:05.63,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,So I've got to take action!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.97,0:04:09.33,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,My, what an admirable attitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.10,0:04:24.68,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Spare me your theatrics.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.60,0:04:28.89,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You've been able to see me \Nall along, haven't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.25,0:04:36.09,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I've no doubt you realized I was there \Nsince we met at the Grand Merillian.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.07,0:04:43.27,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Otherwise, you'd never have bothered with\Nthe engagement of a viscount's daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.08,0:04:47.75,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I have an excellent memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.40,0:04:51.02,Flashback,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Oh, how heartrending!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.01,0:04:52.52,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,10 YEARS AGO
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.33,0:04:56.38,Flashback,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Might your humble servant \Nassist you in any way?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.38,0:04:58.54,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You're an eyesore. Get out of my sight.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.51,0:05:01.66,Flashback,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Oh, what a shame.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.66,0:05:05.38,Flashback,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Should the fancy ever strike you, \Nplease call upon your humble servant.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.38,0:05:07.77,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Yes. {\i1}If{\i0} the fancy strikes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.11,0:05:13.06,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It took ten years, \Nbut the fancy struck me at last.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.54,0:05:14.58,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.39,0:05:17.82,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,lend me your aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.65,0:05:20.05,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,In that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.57,0:05:25.53,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,how may this unworthy hog be of service?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.28,0:05:28.00,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,By hunting rats.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.15,0:05:33.74,Default,Aide,0,0,0,,Your Royal Highness Prince Theophilis,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.33,0:05:36.89,Default,Aide,0,0,0,,Kendall Levine of the \Ndiplomatic service is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.78,0:05:43.33,Default,Theophilis,0,0,0,,What? I thought he left \Non a mission to Adelbide.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.33,0:05:44.20,Default,Aide,0,0,0,,Regarding that,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.61,0:05:46.72,Default,Aide,0,0,0,,he claims there's been\Nan urgent development.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.19,0:05:48.27,Default,Theophilis,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.27,0:05:49.22,Default,Theophilis,0,0,0,,Show him in.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.14,0:05:53.82,Default,Theophilis,0,0,0,,It's been ages, Kendall.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.43,0:05:56.47,Default,Theophilis,0,0,0,,What on earth is the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.92,0:05:58.65,Default,Kendall,0,0,0,,With all due respect,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.65,0:06:04.66,Default,Kendall,0,0,0,,Prince Ulysses was abducted not \Nby Adelbide, but by Daeg Gallus,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.96,0:06:10.92,Default,Kendall,0,0,0,,and Second Prince Roderick \Nis in league with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.92,0:06:12.14,Default,Theophilis,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.14,0:06:14.19,Default,Kendall,0,0,0,,I'm told that every member of Daeg Gallus
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.19,0:06:18.38,Default,Kendall,0,0,0,,bears a tattoo of the sun \Nsomewhere on their bodies.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.38,0:06:19.58,Default,Theophilis,0,0,0,,A tattoo?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.82,0:06:27.45,Default,Theophilis,0,0,0,,I never suspected Roderick!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.88,0:06:31.80,Default,Theophilis,0,0,0,,Where exactly did you \Nget this information?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.80,0:06:36.09,Default,Kendall,0,0,0,,From Third Princess Alexandra.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.11,0:06:39.54,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,In the ordinary course of events,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.54,0:06:44.39,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,I was to receive charity from \NPrince Enrique in the near future.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.79,0:06:46.06,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,Charity?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.54,0:06:50.76,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Indeed. To facilitate \Nspreading the divine word,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.76,0:06:57.07,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,we need "contributions" from the faithful\N more substantial than prayers.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.56,0:07:00.92,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,I doubt that my brother \Nwould do any such thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.92,0:07:02.81,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,You must be mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.81,0:07:07.73,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,You don't say.\N Then pray forgive my intrusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.18,0:07:10.57,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,By the way...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.57,0:07:12.00,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.00,0:07:17.08,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Have you need of divine aid yourself, \NYour Royal Highness?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.63,0:07:18.96,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,Well, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.80,0:07:27.24,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Begging your pardon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.86,0:07:29.87,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Am I interrupting?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.87,0:07:32.71,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,No. The viscount was just leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.71,0:07:34.85,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,And you are...?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.73,0:07:37.23,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Rufus May.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.23,0:07:41.39,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,I was recently appointed \Nassistant comptroller of the treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.39,0:07:44.49,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Why, then you're the man \NI've heard about!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.49,0:07:48.40,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Have you ever visited my church?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.66,0:07:53.01,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,I'm afraid not, as I'm still new \Nto my post. But someday.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.01,0:07:55.40,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Why, we would be delighted to have you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.19,0:08:03.66,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Oh, do forgive me. \NStatic electricity, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.29,0:08:07.78,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,That, or a whim of the goddesses.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.74,0:08:12.22,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Don't you feel pain?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.66,0:08:13.86,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Of course I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.86,0:08:19.18,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,It's merely that any pain you inflict \Nis the greatest of joys to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.34,0:08:24.35,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Now, did anything strike you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.35,0:08:29.44,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That man kept his gloves on, \Neven when you went to shake hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.49,0:08:36.31,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,He has a sun tattoo on his wrist.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.33,0:08:42.60,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Rufus May is a rat. \NUncover his antecedents at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.34,0:08:45.92,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,My lady's wish is my command.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.39,0:08:48.67,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Now then, I can do this much safely...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.86,0:08:53.41,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I always feel sleepy \Nafter using that power.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.41,0:08:56.51,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I suppose I feel fine now \Nbecause I kept it weak earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.76,0:08:58.12,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.12,0:09:02.51,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Causing such phenomena \Nconsumes a great deal of energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.97,0:09:06.02,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,How would you know about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.30,0:09:09.85,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,For all my faults, \NI do have the goddesses' favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.64,0:09:15.95,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,By the way, is revenge your reason \Nfor remaining in this world?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.57,0:09:18.22,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Of course it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.94,0:09:21.12,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Even now?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.12,0:09:22.46,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What are you getting at?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.03,0:09:28.79,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Here and now, are you \Nbeing driven by revenge?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.79,0:09:30.55,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Or...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.55,0:09:33.77,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,are you working to save Constance Grail?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.37,0:09:37.80,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Revenge, naturally.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.80,0:09:39.58,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.58,0:09:43.55,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,I believe that, to remain \Nin the world of the living,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.55,0:09:48.57,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,a disembodied soul must have \Nsome powerful emotion or goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.90,0:09:53.84,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,So I have no doubt that once you feel \Nyour revenge is complete,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.05,0:09:58.21,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,you will return to the gods' side.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.06,0:10:09.70,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Please sign our petition \Nagainst this execution!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.24,0:10:12.87,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Constance Grail is innocent!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.04,0:10:15.09,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.73,0:10:18.35,Default,Ethel,0,0,0,,I beg you. Lend us your aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.44,0:10:24.59,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,Please help us! We can't save \Nmy friend Constance Grail
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.94,0:10:29.10,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,without assistance from\N the right-minded people here!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.45,0:10:32.11,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,What's the meaning of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.37,0:10:36.12,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I gave strict orders to keep \Nany petition out of the palace,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.12,0:10:40.25,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,and not just commoners have signed this.\N Aristocrats are in on it as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.70,0:10:43.51,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Then there's this book...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.25,0:10:49.58,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,It claims to be by an up-and-coming \Nforeign author. Adam Hicks?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.43,0:10:53.60,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,It's obviously Amelia Hobbes!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.60,0:10:56.53,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,A viscount's daughter, lauded as a saint,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.53,0:10:59.84,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,overcomes the gap in status \Nto marry a crown prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.47,0:11:04.23,Default,Krishna,0,0,0,,But in reality, she's a member \Nof a criminal syndicate
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.22,0:11:07.98,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,who was born an impoverished orphan.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.30,0:11:11.05,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,I feel as though \NI've heard this plot before.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.29,0:11:18.74,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Why would they go to such lengths \Nfor that plain little girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.74,0:11:22.23,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,No matter what anyone says, \Nshe {\i1}will{\i0} be executed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.55,0:11:26.49,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Along with that Lucia girl \Nthe O'Brians adopted.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.98,0:11:29.32,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.32,0:11:30.50,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.50,0:11:33.18,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,What an unpleasant state of affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.18,0:11:37.02,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,And just look how those absurd rumors \Nspread when one's not looking.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.44,0:11:38.47,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,What rumors?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.01,0:11:40.51,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Haven't you heard?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.91,0:11:43.03,Default,Krishna,0,0,0,,I mean about Constance Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.40,0:11:47.52,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,They say she can hear \Nthe voices of the dead
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.52,0:11:52.00,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,and that she's working to clear \NScarlett Castiel's name.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.82,0:11:59.02,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Crown Princess Cecilia?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.00,0:12:03.27,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,They say you can speak with the dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.64,0:12:05.31,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,W-Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.95,0:12:07.11,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Liar.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.95,0:12:10.26,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,The dead don't talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.26,0:12:14.16,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,They have no thoughts.\NThey just turn to ashes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.44,0:12:16.91,Main - Italics,Cecilia {M},0,0,0,,It's only natural.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.58,0:12:20.36,Main - Italics,Cecilia {M},0,0,0,,At least, that's how it was for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.59,0:12:24.92,Main - Italics,Cecilia {M},0,0,0,,I've never heard any voices.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.43,0:12:28.74,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Whose voice...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.18,0:12:30.93,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,DID YOU WANT TO HEAR?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.73,0:12:39.19,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,14 YEARS AGO
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.29,0:12:37.69,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Cici!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.69,0:12:39.43,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Go give that back!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.43,0:12:41.55,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,What? Why should I, Cess?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.55,0:12:43.82,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Picking pockets is a crime!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.82,0:12:46.83,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,I'm not letting you lead a life
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.83,0:12:51.33,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,you can't be proud of\Nwhile I've got my eye on you!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.84,0:12:57.57,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Hey, mister!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.08,0:13:02.98,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,You did it! That's my Cici!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.98,0:13:05.47,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Hey, quit it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.38,0:13:09.22,Flashback,Lia,0,0,0,,Cici, Cess! You're back!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.58,0:13:12.20,Flashback,Pete,0,0,0,,Listen, there's this weird guy here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.20,0:13:13.40,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Weird how?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.84,0:13:17.22,Flashback,Lia,0,0,0,,He says he's looking \Nfor a girl named Cecilia!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.22,0:13:20.35,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,He's sure got his work \Ncut out for him, huh, Cess?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.35,0:13:24.87,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Yeah. There's loads of Cecilias, \Neven just at our place.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.87,0:13:27.46,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,You there. You're called Cess?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.85,0:13:30.94,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,Then is your real name Cecilia?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.61,0:13:33.40,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Y-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.61,0:13:38.09,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,Your eyes...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.22,0:13:41.42,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,look rosy in the right light, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.08,0:13:46.17,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,Sister, I'd like to have \Na chat with this girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.35,0:13:56.14,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,He said the lord's daughter was \Nborn sickly and won't live much longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.14,0:14:00.34,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,So I'm going to play \Nthe part of Miss Cecilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.34,0:14:02.09,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Why you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.65,0:14:06.94,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,He said the lord had \Na secret child with a whore.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.94,0:14:10.41,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Her name happened to be Cecilia too,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.78,0:14:14.70,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,and they put her in some orphanage \Nright after she was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.44,0:14:18.27,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Couldn't he have the wrong girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.27,0:14:20.35,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,I mean, that description would fit—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.35,0:14:24.41,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,I don't think he cares \Nwhether I'm the real one or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.78,0:14:27.48,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,I just happen to fit the bill.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.48,0:14:29.70,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,But that doesn't mean you have to...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.70,0:14:33.77,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,He says the lord will donate\N to the orphanage.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.18,0:14:36.86,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,So you'll be just fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.11,0:14:56.83,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Mother Natalie!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.83,0:14:59.79,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Lia! Pete! Everybody!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.85,0:15:03.22,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.59,0:15:04.80,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Cici...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.26,0:15:07.46,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Cess?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.07,0:15:10.85,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Thank goodness! You're alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.16,0:15:12.85,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,What are you doing here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.28,0:15:17.58,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,It's my fault. I was such a fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.58,0:15:18.95,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,What do you mean?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.79,0:15:25.35,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Lord Luze was never going to let anyone \Nwho knew of his replacement daughter live.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.35,0:15:28.49,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,If I'd only realized sooner!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.49,0:15:30.72,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,It's not your fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.12,0:15:34.79,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Can you walk? Where's everyone else?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.79,0:15:39.33,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,They killed them all. \NYou're the only one I didn't see dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.74,0:15:42.44,Flashback,Man A,0,0,0,,Hey! We got a live one over here!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.25,0:15:44.98,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,We'll flee out the back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.47,0:15:53.43,Flashback,Man A,0,0,0,,Where are they?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.43,0:15:54.39,Flashback,Man B,0,0,0,,I'm going after them!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.62,0:16:08.92,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Cess?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.47,0:16:13.03,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Go on ahead! Call for help!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.03,0:16:15.19,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?!\N Come with me!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.19,0:16:19.00,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,They'll never stop chasing you\N now that they've seen you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.79,0:16:22.04,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,I'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.04,0:16:22.91,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Cess!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.42,0:16:24.49,Flashback,Cess,0,0,0,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.18,0:16:43.27,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,All my hard work to find that pawn, \Nonly to have her broken so easily...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.37,0:16:46.67,Flashback,Salvador,0,0,0,,She was supposed to be at the mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.67,0:16:49.69,Flashback,Salvador,0,0,0,,They never would've thought \Nshe'd be at the orphanage.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.61,0:16:54.02,Flashback,Salvador,0,0,0,,This is all because Viscount Luze \Ntried to take matters into his own hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.02,0:16:56.68,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,Nobles of his ilk are all the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.45,0:17:00.81,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,What's this? A survivor?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.57,0:17:03.57,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.29,0:17:05.59,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Cici.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.55,0:17:07.66,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.69,0:17:09.99,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,A girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.51,0:17:15.44,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,Come to think of it,\N "Cici" was another nickname for Cecilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.64,0:17:19.68,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,And you have perfect rosy eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.48,0:17:22.70,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,The mark of the Luze family.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.70,0:17:25.61,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,I missed it because I took you for a boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.94,0:17:30.34,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,I got the sense that girl \Nwas hiding something.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.34,0:17:33.61,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,Now I see it was you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.61,0:17:39.79,Flashback - Italics,Cici {M},0,0,0,,Cess went with that lord to protect me!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.60,0:17:42.77,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,Do you hate Viscount Luze?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.25,0:17:44.13,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,In that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.77,0:17:47.21,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,what do you say I help you take revenge?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.75,0:17:50.42,Flashback,Cici,0,0,0,,Revenge...?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.50,0:17:54.76,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,If you do as we say,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.10,0:17:58.51,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,we'll let you make that lowlife \Nsuffer like you wouldn't believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.32,0:18:03.22,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,Just do what your heart tells you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.22,0:18:05.99,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,Don't you hate him?\N Don't you want to make him pay?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.99,0:18:09.76,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,So just tear him down.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.08,0:18:11.72,Flashback,Krishna,0,0,0,,And this country with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.97,0:18:18.11,Flashback - Italics,Cess,0,0,0,,You did it! That's my Cici!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.48,0:18:19.67,Flashback - Top + Italics,Cici,0,0,0,,Hey, quit it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.67,0:18:22.53,Flashback - Italics,Cess,0,0,0,,It's my fault. I was such a fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.93,0:18:24.16,Flashback - Top + Italics,Cici,0,0,0,,It's not your fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.91,0:18:31.13,Flashback - Italics,Cess,0,0,0,,I'm going to play \Nthe part of Miss Cecilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.96,0:18:38.93,Main - Italics,Cecilia {M},0,0,0,,I don't...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.18,0:18:42.73,Main - Italics,Cecilia {M},0,0,0,,want to hear anyone's voice anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.71,0:18:46.67,Default,Krishna,0,0,0,,Oh, that reminds me. I've decided.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.16,0:18:49.91,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Decided what?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.84,0:18:55.20,Default,Krishna,0,0,0,,I told you. When to kill the O'Brian girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.05,0:19:01.24,Default,Krishna,0,0,0,,I thought we might as well make it \Nthe day of Constance Grail's execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.87,0:19:03.13,Default,Krishna,0,0,0,,The day after tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.93,0:19:04.94,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.21,0:19:09.76,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Did you find out anything about Rufus?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.76,0:19:15.90,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,It appears the real Rufus May \Npassed away ten years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.25,0:19:19.28,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,He was the youngest child \Nof less-than-wealthy nobles.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.28,0:19:25.34,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,He came to the capital when his bad \Nconduct effectively got him disowned.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.34,0:19:27.06,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Ten years ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.06,0:19:30.86,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I see. So they replaced him back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.62,0:19:38.35,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,Rest a little. I know you \Nhaven't been sleeping.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.99,0:19:40.52,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.84,0:19:45.63,Default,San,0,0,0,,Whoops. Am I interrupting something?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.11,0:19:47.94,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,No, that's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.75,0:19:55.50,Default,San,0,0,0,,Like I told you, Princess Alexandra\N of Faris opposes war.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.84,0:19:59.83,Default,San,0,0,0,,Wouldn't you like to see her \Naccede to the throne?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.25,0:20:05.00,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,Your third princess has no lineage \Nor support worth mentioning.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.68,0:20:08.65,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,Plus, isn't she a prisoner \Nin Faris right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.51,0:20:12.86,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,I don't see what chance \Nshe has of winning out.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.27,0:20:16.90,Default,San,0,0,0,,But what if she got herself \Na major backer?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.46,0:20:21.93,Default,San,0,0,0,,What if King Ernst only {\i1}said{\i0} he was \Ngoing to talk trade with Melvina,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.93,0:20:23.95,Default,San,0,0,0,,while really he went to Faris?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.65,0:20:26.01,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.01,0:20:28.41,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,But the king has no reason to go there.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.41,0:20:32.54,Default,San,0,0,0,,He could always say he's paying \Nthe king of Faris a get-well visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.03,0:20:38.67,Default,San,0,0,0,,Only the fact that the captive \Nthird princess invited him would matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.20,0:20:43.42,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I see. Word would spread on its own.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.81,0:20:47.06,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Word that Adelbide is allied \Nwith the third princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.06,0:20:50.64,Default,San,0,0,0,,Exactly. And just like that,\N she'd have support.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.30,0:20:54.62,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,But isn't the third princess locked up?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.62,0:20:57.32,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,How is she going to invite the king?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.89,0:21:01.44,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Unless... the princess \Nin the tower is a double?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.19,0:21:06.96,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,Hang on! You mean you're swaying \Nthe whole nation with a bluff?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.96,0:21:11.10,Default,San,0,0,0,,It just goes to show how much \NFaris fears your country.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.59,0:21:18.62,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Why didn't Crown Princess Cecilia \Ngive me any answer at all?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.78,0:21:21.14,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,You have a visitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.21,0:21:26.67,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Is that you, Brenda?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.35,0:21:34.54,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Well, um... What brings you here?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.14,0:21:36.21,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,Look.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.13,0:21:40.70,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Kate and Mylene are \Nprotesting my execution?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.70,0:21:43.37,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,Th-They aren't alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.37,0:21:50.33,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,Your father, your ex-fiancé Neil Bronson,\Nand Viscount Hamsworth are all helping.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.33,0:21:53.05,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,And the Earl of Ulster, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.05,0:21:54.27,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,His Lordship!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.62,0:21:58.93,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Tell me, Brenda, when am I to be executed?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.38,0:22:01.97,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, they say.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.90,0:22:04.44,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.02,0:22:11.85,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,Listen, I'm... thinking \Nof accusing Pamela.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.05,0:22:16.11,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,I'll testify to everything\N she's ever done!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.06,0:22:19.37,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,It's too little, too late, I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.86,0:22:23.61,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,I've... I've been wanting \Nto tell you something all this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.35,0:22:28.26,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,Thank you for saving me back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.03,0:22:32.25,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,That wasn't me, Brenda. It was—
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.25,0:22:34.37,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,No, it was you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.92,0:22:39.37,Default,Brenda,0,0,0,,Your sincerity saved me.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.14,0:22:44.62,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,I'm not alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.49,0:22:47.74,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Everyone is fighting for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.88,0:22:50.88,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,I'll never give up.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.42,0:22:52.52,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,After all...
